{{also|shake down|shake-down}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|shake-down}}

===Etymology===
From the verb phrase {{m|en|shake down}}. An improvised bed would originally have been made by shaking down straw.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-shakedown.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} [[extortion|Extortion]], especially through [[blackmail]]
#: ''What is this, a '''shakedown'''?''
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2021-08-25/video-sparks-arrest-of-thai-police-in-drug-suspect-s-death|title=Four Thai Police Charged in Drug Suspect’s Death After Video Surfaces|work=Bloomberg|publisher=Bloomberg|date=2021-08-25|accessdate=2021-08-25|text=Four Thai police officers charged with murder in connection with the deadly '''shakedown''' of a suspected drug dealer in custody were arrested Wednesday after a video clip of the incident shared on social media caused a public furor.|author=Tassanee Vejpongsa}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[thorough]] [[search]]; a [[frisk]]
# A [[trial]] or [[test]] [[period]], especially of a [[ship]] or [[aircraft]]
# An improvised [[bed]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=79|passage=All sorts of gossip floated about; one story told was that a selector, and not the youngest of that staid and sober party, was found putting his boots into his '''shakedown''' at night, and lying outside the entrance of his tent, giving careful directions to some one to call him in time for the morning mail.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1915|author={{w|W. Somerset Maugham}}|title=[[s:Of Human Bondage/Chapter_CXIV|Of Human Bondage]]
|passage="There's nowhere for me to lie down, sir," he answered, and there was in his voice a humbleness which was very distressing. -- "Don't you know anyone in the house who'll give you a '''shakedown'''?" -- "No, sir."}}
#*'''1974''', {{w|Thea Astley}}, ''A Kindness Cup'', Text Classics 2018, p. 107:
#*:‘You two,’ he says, ‘you're not going back tonight. […] I can make you '''shake-downs''' on the veranda and we'll have a bite to eat.’

